1
00:02:22,973 --> 00:02:26,045
<i>- So how's your mom, Ton?
- Same.</i>

2
00:02:26,293 --> 00:02:32,163
<i>But my ex-goomar's cousin, I got her
to take care of her. Russian girl.</i>

3
00:02:32,373 --> 00:02:36,844
<i>Who was telling me the Bevilaqua
kid has money from construction?</i>

4
00:02:37,093 --> 00:02:41,405
<i>- Fucking Matthew was never any good.
- He sure cried like a baby.</i>

5
00:02:41,613 --> 00:02:44,923
<i>I think the family was relieved
he got taken out.</i>

6
00:02:45,133 --> 00:02:46,771
<i>What are you gonna eat?</i>

7
00:02:46,973 --> 00:02:48,929
<i>Hey, waiter!</i>

8
00:02:50,693 --> 00:02:55,562
That's the closest CW16 got Tony
to discussing the Bevilaqua murder?

9
00:02:55,773 --> 00:03:00,324
I think at this point it's time
to consider 16, Bonpensiero, compost.

10
00:03:01,173 --> 00:03:06,088
Bonpensiero was crucial
to the Webistics stock fraud case.

11
00:03:06,293 --> 00:03:08,329
So RICO-wise...

12
00:03:09,333 --> 00:03:12,405
...the airline tickets,
mail and wire fraud...

13
00:03:12,613 --> 00:03:15,207
...if the mother testifies
for immunity.

14
00:03:15,413 --> 00:03:17,768
Whose own mother's gonna testify?

15
00:03:18,293 --> 00:03:21,330
I say focus on his garbage business.

16
00:03:21,533 --> 00:03:26,209
- Extortion. Interstate trucking.
- It'll yield a prosecutable murder.

17
00:03:26,613 --> 00:03:30,845
Richie Aprile, no doubt about it,
the cartel had him whacked.

18
00:03:31,093 --> 00:03:34,847
But Tony shows diligence
when it comes to debugging.

19
00:03:35,533 --> 00:03:40,049
- What about the home?
- They talked in the basement.

20
00:03:40,253 --> 00:03:43,768
His own basement?
Where's the due diligence there?

21
00:03:44,013 --> 00:03:45,969
Tony avoids business at home.

22
00:03:46,213 --> 00:03:51,333
He'll take somebody out by the pool.
Except there he fears parabolics.

23
00:03:51,533 --> 00:03:57,529
The basement has noisy AC ducts.
He turns on the air and he feels safe.

24
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:03,771
"Surreptitiously enter and leave. "
A "sneak and peek" warrant.

25
00:04:04,013 --> 00:04:07,130
- Correct.
- I said you could enter the basement.

26
00:04:07,333 --> 00:04:10,006
Do we have to impact
this family's privacy?

27
00:04:10,253 --> 00:04:14,326
First we determine
where to best place the wire.

28
00:04:14,573 --> 00:04:19,442
Then the listening device
will be fabricated and we install it.

29
00:04:19,693 --> 00:04:23,208
See that they limit both
entrances to the basement.

30
00:04:23,413 --> 00:04:26,644
<i>It's not a Better Homes
and Gardens tour.</i>

31
00:04:28,013 --> 00:04:29,526
Happy hunting.

32
00:04:41,893 --> 00:04:46,330
<i>You know, the coffeemaker's got
to be plugged in for it to work!</i>

33
00:04:47,733 --> 00:04:49,963
Same time as yesterday.

34
00:04:55,213 --> 00:04:58,125
I'm just going to the
stationery store.

35
00:04:58,333 --> 00:05:02,406
I'll be right back.
You don't gotta follow me. All right?

36
00:05:05,213 --> 00:05:10,048
To drop a wire there's got to be
nobody home for at least two hours.

37
00:05:10,253 --> 00:05:12,892
The maid is gone
on Tuesday afternoons.

38
00:05:13,133 --> 00:05:16,523
- Why?
- Classes to get her U.S. Citizenship.

39
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:19,122
She's gone from 1 till about 2:45.

40
00:05:19,453 --> 00:05:22,968
Class, then she and
her husband have lunch.

41
00:05:23,213 --> 00:05:26,046
He's applying for citizenship too.

42
00:05:26,413 --> 00:05:28,529
What's his name again?

43
00:05:28,973 --> 00:05:33,728
- Stasiu Wosilius.
- I'll run that by Anti-Terrorism.

44
00:05:33,973 --> 00:05:36,533
Carmela's gone on Tuesday. Tennis.

45
00:05:36,733 --> 00:05:41,648
We need somebody on her and everybody
that's got a key to the house.

46
00:05:41,853 --> 00:05:43,605
Daughter's at Columbia.

47
00:05:43,813 --> 00:05:47,726
Why risk it? She's 45 minutes
away. Put somebody on her.

48
00:05:47,973 --> 00:05:52,728
Anyone breaks for home, we need
to warn the team to get the hell out.

49
00:06:27,413 --> 00:06:32,362
<i>- Unit 1, Baby Bing headed your way.
- Copy, control.</i>

50
00:06:55,893 --> 00:06:59,329
Unit 2, you got Bada Bing
headed your way.

51
00:07:00,333 --> 00:07:03,291
Excuse me. Unit 3,
Mrs. Bing also in motion.

52
00:07:27,333 --> 00:07:32,327
<i>- Do you have contact of Princess Bing?
- Roger, control.</i>

53
00:07:43,413 --> 00:07:46,052
Unit 4, here comes the maid.
Gray Jetta.

54
00:07:46,293 --> 00:07:50,206
S.E. Team, the location's secure.
You have 90 minutes.

55
00:08:06,573 --> 00:08:09,724
Control, we're headed
into the sausage factory.

56
00:08:58,893 --> 00:09:01,088
- Just in time.
- Set a plate.

57
00:09:01,293 --> 00:09:02,726
You got it.

58
00:09:02,973 --> 00:09:07,046
I had him darn it in the shoulder,
like she wanted.

59
00:09:07,253 --> 00:09:10,484
- It shouldn't have torn.
- Beautiful coat.

60
00:09:10,693 --> 00:09:14,368
- What the fuck? Lunch is ready.
- I wash my hands.

61
00:09:14,613 --> 00:09:17,252
- You washed your hands.
- I tied my shoe.

62
00:09:17,453 --> 00:09:20,763
- So what?
- I can't stand touching shoelaces.

63
00:09:20,973 --> 00:09:25,171
Ever tie your shoes and notice
the ends of your laces are wet?

64
00:09:25,373 --> 00:09:29,525
- From what? Why would they be wet?
- I got no fucking idea.

65
00:09:29,773 --> 00:09:33,368
- You stand at the urinals...
- Come on, will you?

66
00:09:33,613 --> 00:09:36,332
He's asking, I'm telling.
It's important.

67
00:09:36,533 --> 00:09:40,082
Even if the lace is dry
and you don't touch the shoe.

68
00:09:40,293 --> 00:09:43,649
- Bacteria and virus migrate.
- You see this on TV?

69
00:09:43,893 --> 00:09:49,126
I gotta watch TV to figure out the
world? A men's shithouse is a sewer.

70
00:09:49,333 --> 00:09:53,849
In ladies' johns, you could eat
maple ice cream from the toilets.

71
00:09:54,053 --> 00:09:57,250
There's exceptions. But a men's?

72
00:09:57,493 --> 00:10:02,044
Piss all over the fucking floor.
Urinals jammed with cigarettes.

73
00:10:02,293 --> 00:10:06,730
They can pour all the ice they want,
it does nothing to kill germs.

74
00:10:06,973 --> 00:10:12,252
- Even if you don't drag the laces.
- Shut the fuck up!

75
00:10:14,573 --> 00:10:19,328
Mission control, I'm disabling
the line to the phone company.

76
00:10:21,213 --> 00:10:24,888
Phone line to the alarm
is neutralized. Cut it.

77
00:10:25,093 --> 00:10:28,005
Hold your breath.
I'm clipping the siren.

78
00:10:29,693 --> 00:10:31,923
Pick it, Wilson.

79
00:10:34,613 --> 00:10:39,004
<i>Control, we're working on entry.
Estimate three to four minutes.</i>

80
00:10:54,213 --> 00:10:56,204
You're not hungry?

81
00:10:57,093 --> 00:11:00,529
<i>- Have some braciole.
- No, thanks.</i>

82
00:11:00,733 --> 00:11:03,327
I got no appetite.

83
00:11:04,813 --> 00:11:08,328
- Today would've been our birthday.
- "Our" birthday?

84
00:11:10,213 --> 00:11:12,124
Oh, yeah.

85
00:11:12,373 --> 00:11:13,852
Spoons.

86
00:11:15,133 --> 00:11:18,091
- Happy birthday. How old are you?
- 51.

87
00:11:18,293 --> 00:11:20,329
Who came first, you or Spoons?

88
00:11:20,573 --> 00:11:23,690
Philip was my kid brother
by 11 minutes.

89
00:11:23,893 --> 00:11:26,726
Hey, it was a fucking tragedy.

90
00:11:27,733 --> 00:11:29,451
What're you gonna do?

91
00:11:29,653 --> 00:11:34,727
- It's the life we chose. Right, Pat?
- But my brother was never a heavy guy.

92
00:11:34,973 --> 00:11:38,522
I mean he was a sweet, gentle man.

93
00:11:39,013 --> 00:11:42,449
- Your brother was your twin brother?
- Philly.

94
00:11:42,933 --> 00:11:48,883
Friends, like us, called him Spoons.
Somebody whacked the kid.

95
00:11:49,573 --> 00:11:51,006
Before you came over.

96
00:11:51,213 --> 00:11:54,523
You big-mouthed fuck! Fuck!

97
00:11:55,373 --> 00:12:00,970
- You identical twin? Or the other kind?
- Identical.

98
00:12:01,213 --> 00:12:03,932
Here, have something to eat.

99
00:12:04,493 --> 00:12:09,965
There's a twin bond. Unless you
experienced it, you can't understand.

100
00:12:10,173 --> 00:12:13,848
- Okay with onions?
- Maybe it sounds crazy to you.

101
00:12:14,413 --> 00:12:18,326
Hey, nothing sounds crazy anymore.
The older I get...

102
00:12:18,813 --> 00:12:21,043
It's over, right?

103
00:12:25,773 --> 00:12:30,369
Don't it happen that twins can
die within days of each other?

104
00:12:30,613 --> 00:12:35,562
- That would've been okay, believe me.
- Come on! God forbid!

105
00:12:37,333 --> 00:12:41,929
- I miss him so much.
- Well, that's natural.

106
00:12:42,213 --> 00:12:46,331
You're with us. Leave the morbid
shit back at Junior's crew...

107
00:12:46,693 --> 00:12:48,524
...and have a happy birthday.

108
00:12:49,573 --> 00:12:51,325
Happy birthday.

109
00:12:51,573 --> 00:12:56,693
<i>You wanna commit suicide? Tie your
shoes and have a bite of braciole.</i>

110
00:12:58,733 --> 00:13:01,930
<i>Hey, stonato, it's a joke. Come on!</i>

111
00:13:07,613 --> 00:13:08,841
Hello!

112
00:13:10,213 --> 00:13:14,729
- God, don't transfer me now.
- Adriana La Cerva.

113
00:13:17,413 --> 00:13:19,973
How green was my fucking valley.

114
00:13:21,453 --> 00:13:22,647
Hi, Ed.

115
00:13:23,533 --> 00:13:27,242
This is my friend.
Adriana La Cerva, Ed Restuccia.

116
00:13:27,493 --> 00:13:32,362
I'm delighted to teach a pal of Carm's.
My most disciplined student.

117
00:13:32,613 --> 00:13:35,286
Perfect muscle tone
doesn't hurt either.

118
00:13:35,893 --> 00:13:38,168
I have to apologize, Carm.

119
00:13:38,413 --> 00:13:43,362
I thought I called everybody.
I won't be teaching here anymore.

120
00:13:43,613 --> 00:13:45,922
- Everything's all right?
- Basically.

121
00:13:46,133 --> 00:13:50,445
Kitty got this dot-com job
in San Diego, so we're moving.

122
00:13:50,693 --> 00:13:54,129
- I didn't even know you were married.
- Yeah.

123
00:13:54,813 --> 00:13:57,532
But you're in luck.
Birgit is taking over.

124
00:13:57,733 --> 00:14:01,169
- How wonderful.
- I never even played once.

125
00:14:01,373 --> 00:14:02,806
That's why you're here.

126
00:14:03,013 --> 00:14:07,529
Carm, I was wondering about
letters of recommendation...

127
00:14:17,093 --> 00:14:21,644
Kitty's company sells antiques,
so if you wanted a piece...

128
00:14:22,173 --> 00:14:26,644
- No antiques. My house is traditional.
- I'm cutting into your lesson.

129
00:14:26,893 --> 00:14:29,805
- Carmela, bye. Nice meeting you.
- Take care.

130
00:14:42,533 --> 00:14:45,445
Baby Bing is leaving school property.
On it.

131
00:14:47,573 --> 00:14:49,131
- Taking orders.
- Snapple.

132
00:14:49,373 --> 00:14:52,331
- Me too.
- I only got 2 bucks.

133
00:14:53,613 --> 00:14:55,763
Mrs. Celeste almost saw my board.

134
00:14:56,013 --> 00:15:00,723
- What a retard rule: "No boards. "
- They can't see how useful boards are.

135
00:15:00,973 --> 00:15:05,046
In the cafeteria, each person
could just roll past the food...

136
00:15:05,253 --> 00:15:07,972
...and make their decisions.
- Yeah.

137
00:15:08,133 --> 00:15:09,930
That food tastes like ass.

138
00:15:17,133 --> 00:15:18,452
Hit it!

139
00:15:29,173 --> 00:15:31,733
- I had enough for one.
- Give me a hit.

140
00:15:31,973 --> 00:15:34,043
Don't backwash.

141
00:15:34,853 --> 00:15:39,449
- I won't do anything for this school.
- Mom's all, "Get involved. "

142
00:15:39,653 --> 00:15:42,406
- I am. With boarding.
- It's Egon.

143
00:15:42,613 --> 00:15:43,807
Hey, Kosma!

144
00:15:50,413 --> 00:15:52,324
- Where you been?
- Orthodontist.

145
00:15:53,533 --> 00:15:55,922
- What class you ditching?
- Assembly.

146
00:15:56,173 --> 00:15:58,164
- Excellent jersey.
- Yeah.

147
00:15:58,413 --> 00:16:01,246
- Wait. You went out for JV ball?
- Yeah.

148
00:16:01,493 --> 00:16:05,452
Mr. Quadriplegic, remind me
not to visit you in the hospital.

149
00:16:05,653 --> 00:16:08,725
- That is a cool shirt.
- Yeah.

150
00:16:09,773 --> 00:16:12,765
- What position?
- Douche bag.

151
00:16:27,813 --> 00:16:29,041
Okay, cut it!

152
00:16:48,613 --> 00:16:50,569
Y'all should have come.

153
00:16:51,773 --> 00:16:55,652
- Where'd you go?
- We started off at Smoke's, as usual.

154
00:16:55,893 --> 00:16:58,646
But we wound up
at this place, Ruby Foo's...

155
00:16:58,893 --> 00:17:02,806
...round Broadway and 65th,
or something.

156
00:17:03,333 --> 00:17:07,565
It was so fun.
God, did I get hammered!

157
00:17:08,413 --> 00:17:13,567
- Don't you have a quiz today?
- Frosh Week. What do they expect?

158
00:17:14,173 --> 00:17:20,043
- I'll study now.
- I have a bio lab. I haven't read it.

159
00:17:21,773 --> 00:17:25,846
- Still miss New Jersey?
- It's only, like, half an hour away.

160
00:17:26,053 --> 00:17:29,363
It's just this transition.
It's a lot of work.

161
00:17:29,573 --> 00:17:34,044
New York is an experience
that unalterably changes a person.

162
00:17:34,253 --> 00:17:39,247
- It is really great.
- And all this freedom of college.

163
00:17:48,293 --> 00:17:52,809
- When did you have your last cocktail?
- 11:30 this morning.

164
00:17:53,413 --> 00:17:55,927
Jesus, Caitlin.

165
00:18:13,053 --> 00:18:18,730
- What is the most important right?
- Right to vote.

166
00:18:20,773 --> 00:18:25,324
Special capers from Italy.
Soprano kids don't like them.

167
00:18:26,413 --> 00:18:29,928
- Who wrote "The Star-Spangled Banner"?
- Martin Luther King.

168
00:18:30,173 --> 00:18:34,007
- Stasiu, you know this.
- I want to eat.

169
00:18:35,453 --> 00:18:36,932
Francis Scott Key.

170
00:18:40,773 --> 00:18:44,561
What holiday was celebrated
by the American colonists?

171
00:18:44,813 --> 00:18:47,122
- Martin Luther King.
- Stasiu!

172
00:18:47,373 --> 00:18:52,572
That's answer to number 49.
"Who was civil rights leader?"

173
00:18:55,213 --> 00:18:58,523
- Which sandwich is for you?
- I don't care.

174
00:19:12,933 --> 00:19:16,562
- Ready.
- Start shooting over here.

175
00:19:17,733 --> 00:19:22,853
Back in Lodz, I was an engineer
with 20 employees...

176
00:19:23,213 --> 00:19:27,729
...and a grant from the state
to do autonomous research.

177
00:19:27,933 --> 00:19:29,969
It bores you?

178
00:19:34,373 --> 00:19:38,605
Don't take those out. Put them
with capers. I take them home.

179
00:19:50,893 --> 00:19:52,770
That's just for Anthony Jr.

180
00:19:53,213 --> 00:19:57,092
- They're expecting WWlll.
- More likely the Colombo wars.

181
00:19:58,533 --> 00:20:02,367
He's got the Black & Decker.
I got one of those.

182
00:20:08,573 --> 00:20:12,691
- 120-gallon water heater.
- My house, we shiver after showers.

183
00:20:13,413 --> 00:20:16,769
Wait a minute. Go back.

184
00:20:17,413 --> 00:20:19,529
Look at the brown water, there.

185
00:20:19,773 --> 00:20:21,729
- What, Ike?
- You don't see it?

186
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:26,164
Creep forward.
Give us some magnification.

187
00:20:27,053 --> 00:20:28,566
That baby's gonna blow.

188
00:20:28,813 --> 00:20:31,850
Tony got about six months
left on that lining.

189
00:20:32,573 --> 00:20:38,330
- A shame we can't warn him.
- During his trial we can inform him.

190
00:20:38,533 --> 00:20:42,731
Except that's at least a year
from now. By that time, boom!

191
00:20:43,893 --> 00:20:46,612
Okay, now you see that lamp there?

192
00:21:03,733 --> 00:21:08,727
- Is that the C-140 microphone?
- They took sound readings. That's new.

193
00:21:08,973 --> 00:21:14,605
They talk where the AC is loudest.
That's where we're placing it.

194
00:21:37,333 --> 00:21:39,927
When's this puppy going in?

195
00:21:40,333 --> 00:21:41,686
Tomorrow.

196
00:22:01,733 --> 00:22:07,729
Okay, fellas and gals, our big day.
As I speak I have Baby Bing, on time.

197
00:22:08,293 --> 00:22:10,045
Handing off to you, George.

198
00:22:17,213 --> 00:22:20,523
<i>I'm on Baby Bing's carpool vehicle.</i>

199
00:22:28,813 --> 00:22:34,251
Furio Giunta Cadillac returning.
Went past me about five minutes ago.

200
00:22:34,493 --> 00:22:37,769
Der Bingle's up early.
He's in the Cadoo.

201
00:22:38,013 --> 00:22:41,801
<i>- Copied. I got the handoff.
- Roger that.</i>

202
00:23:05,573 --> 00:23:08,724
- How's the stock doing?
- Up three at the close.

203
00:23:08,973 --> 00:23:11,931
- Another two so far today.
- Beautiful.

204
00:23:12,173 --> 00:23:15,688
Listen, Ton,
I think we may have a problem.

205
00:23:15,893 --> 00:23:19,727
Log off. That cookie shit
makes me nervous.

206
00:23:20,413 --> 00:23:23,962
We may have a problem
about our friend, the twin.

207
00:23:24,133 --> 00:23:25,327
Yeah, so?

208
00:23:25,493 --> 00:23:28,530
Joey Fleiss hangs out at The Nest,
in Bloomfield.

209
00:23:28,773 --> 00:23:30,365
- Chip's place.
- Yeah.

210
00:23:30,733 --> 00:23:35,329
Our friend is a fixture there.
Joey says he's been into the booze.

211
00:23:35,533 --> 00:23:39,446
He's all fucked up.
They had to pick him up off the floor.

212
00:23:39,653 --> 00:23:45,569
Chip went to him. "Pat, what the fuck?
Can I do anything?" Etcetera.

213
00:23:45,813 --> 00:23:51,524
Pat launches this diatribe about how
one can smile and still be a villain.

214
00:23:51,773 --> 00:23:56,449
And that he knows how his brother
died and who's responsible.

215
00:23:56,693 --> 00:23:59,969
- He mention me by name?
- No. Me neither.

216
00:24:02,333 --> 00:24:05,689
- Hearing this?
- How would he know we clipped Spoons?

217
00:24:05,893 --> 00:24:09,886
- Twin telepathy?
- Somebody's putting ideas in his head.

218
00:24:15,413 --> 00:24:21,124
- Don't let us interfere with your game.
- May be a cop trying to flip him.

219
00:24:21,333 --> 00:24:25,121
Getting him worked up with theories.

220
00:24:27,413 --> 00:24:29,973
- He was talking weird.
- What do we do?

221
00:24:30,173 --> 00:24:33,927
We brought him over from Junior
to keep an eye on him.

222
00:24:34,373 --> 00:24:37,092
So that's what we'll keep doing.

223
00:24:37,293 --> 00:24:40,729
Make no mistake,
part of this guy loves you.

224
00:24:40,973 --> 00:24:43,771
But it's gotta be hard
coming in to work...

225
00:24:43,973 --> 00:24:47,966
...looking in the eyes of the guy
who had your brother whacked.

226
00:24:48,213 --> 00:24:50,932
And even having to smile.

227
00:24:51,373 --> 00:24:53,728
We always have the option.

228
00:24:59,733 --> 00:25:02,327
Mrs. Bing in motion.

229
00:25:03,013 --> 00:25:06,005
We got the housekeeper
then it's all yours.

230
00:25:19,573 --> 00:25:24,124
Hit low to high, Carmela!
And think about your grip.

231
00:25:24,933 --> 00:25:26,366
Fuck!

232
00:25:26,573 --> 00:25:30,361
No, that's good. Nice extension.

233
00:25:30,573 --> 00:25:32,643
Racket back, Carmela!
Come on!

234
00:25:37,293 --> 00:25:39,124
- Fuck.
- No, that's good.

235
00:25:39,373 --> 00:25:42,604
- Shouldn't that housekeeper be out?
- Take a look.

236
00:25:45,333 --> 00:25:47,528
Okay, guys, collect.

237
00:25:47,733 --> 00:25:51,646
Ade, let me work with you here.
Carm, you collect.

238
00:26:05,573 --> 00:26:08,929
Maid's car is still here.

239
00:26:12,133 --> 00:26:18,402
Okay, let's just focus.
Be serious and follow through.

240
00:26:19,013 --> 00:26:21,243
- Right! Almost.
- Okay.

241
00:26:28,933 --> 00:26:32,323
- Did you hear something?
- I don't know.

242
00:26:36,693 --> 00:26:41,369
We think we heard something
from inside the sausage factory.

243
00:26:41,573 --> 00:26:43,211
<i>Hold your position.</i>

244
00:26:46,413 --> 00:26:48,131
- Stand up straight.
- Okay.

245
00:26:48,333 --> 00:26:49,561
Here you go.

246
00:26:49,813 --> 00:26:54,250
See? Low to high.
All right, I can't do this with you.

247
00:26:54,493 --> 00:26:56,529
- Okay.
- Sorry.

248
00:27:11,133 --> 00:27:13,522
She's leaving the court.

249
00:27:24,373 --> 00:27:27,524
Der Bingle's leaving the Bing too.

250
00:27:32,813 --> 00:27:34,724
Hey, watch it!

251
00:27:41,013 --> 00:27:46,326
This does not look good. Mrs. Bing
bearing north on Grand View Avenue.

252
00:27:49,213 --> 00:27:53,331
She's on Boxwood Road.
She's heading toward the factory.

253
00:27:58,013 --> 00:28:02,404
Abort. Repeat, abort!
S.E. Team, get the hell out of there.

254
00:28:02,613 --> 00:28:07,323
<i>Abort, Andy. It's not a go.
Repeat, we are not a go.</i>

255
00:28:23,813 --> 00:28:28,568
- Must be a crisis with a kid.
- I place Baby Bing in the school.

256
00:28:29,493 --> 00:28:32,769
<i>- Unit 5, report.
- A big Roger from this end too.</i>

257
00:28:33,013 --> 00:28:37,882
She went in her room.
She told a friend she was gonna sleep.

258
00:28:38,093 --> 00:28:41,563
<i>- Think somebody made us?
- I don't know.</i>

259
00:28:41,773 --> 00:28:45,288
But we're finished for today,
ladies and gentlemen.

260
00:28:52,413 --> 00:28:58,363
Ten years. Ten fucking years he said
this thing would last! Motherfuck!

261
00:28:58,613 --> 00:29:04,131
- You said that. What are you doing?
- I told you not to put this shit here!

262
00:29:08,573 --> 00:29:10,404
Fuck!

263
00:29:10,613 --> 00:29:14,526
- Fuck!
- Never mind that. Save the pictures.

264
00:29:24,413 --> 00:29:27,564
The prom. Look at this.
Fucking ruined.

265
00:29:27,813 --> 00:29:33,524
- Mr. Ruggerio, thank God.
- The fucking water heater blew.

266
00:29:33,773 --> 00:29:37,322
Your guarantee's
gotta be expired by now.

267
00:29:38,213 --> 00:29:39,692
<i>Madonna.</i>

268
00:29:41,213 --> 00:29:44,171
- Do we have any idea what went down?
- No.

269
00:29:44,413 --> 00:29:47,371
- Family emergency.
- Plumber went there.

270
00:29:47,573 --> 00:29:51,327
Look, we don't have any idea
what happened.

271
00:29:51,493 --> 00:29:53,484
So let's not speculate.

272
00:29:54,133 --> 00:29:56,886
We're shit out of luck till Tuesday.

273
00:29:57,133 --> 00:30:00,443
We'll send somebody there
to stake the house out.

274
00:30:00,693 --> 00:30:03,366
Maybe we got a long-term problem.

275
00:30:03,613 --> 00:30:06,047
Well, we're heading back to Quantico.

276
00:30:06,213 --> 00:30:09,523
We got a job in Denver
day after tomorrow.

277
00:30:09,813 --> 00:30:12,122
A mosque.

278
00:30:18,453 --> 00:30:23,971
Morning. We'd like to get onto
your property to trim some growth...

279
00:30:24,213 --> 00:30:28,092
...that's posing a safety hazard
with the power lines.

280
00:30:28,293 --> 00:30:31,285
Okay. Go around the side.

281
00:30:31,493 --> 00:30:36,283
Records show our repair department
had some crews here yesterday.

282
00:30:36,493 --> 00:30:41,009
- Were you affected by the shortfalls?
- Yesterday?

283
00:30:42,813 --> 00:30:45,122
No.

284
00:30:45,973 --> 00:30:51,969
The people next door had some trucks
go up there. But, no, we're fine.

285
00:30:52,333 --> 00:30:56,485
How about them? Do you know
if everything's okay over there?

286
00:30:56,853 --> 00:30:59,128
As far as I know.

287
00:30:59,773 --> 00:31:03,891
- Well, we'll go talk to them.
- Probably you should.

288
00:31:04,973 --> 00:31:07,441
- They're in the M...
- Pardon?

289
00:31:09,653 --> 00:31:13,282
Nothing. They're different.

290
00:31:13,653 --> 00:31:17,487
For this neighborhood,
they're different, that's all.

291
00:31:17,973 --> 00:31:21,727
- Well, we'll get busy in the back.
- Thanks.

292
00:31:28,973 --> 00:31:32,807
- Still nothing out of the ordinary.
- Is the kid home sick?

293
00:31:34,973 --> 00:31:38,124
I don't see him. I see an arm,
piece of robe...

294
00:31:38,373 --> 00:31:42,252
...it could be Tony.
He's eating Sugar Pops.

295
00:31:42,773 --> 00:31:47,324
Wait, somebody just walked past
the kitchen window. It's the maid.

296
00:31:49,093 --> 00:31:51,527
- They're good.
- Fresh this morning.

297
00:31:51,733 --> 00:31:56,329
- How are things on Bloomfield?
- The Cuban was at the casino.

298
00:31:56,733 --> 00:32:01,170
Big John's okay with a 60-40 split
because we own the building.

299
00:32:01,653 --> 00:32:03,371
- What the hell?
- What?

300
00:32:09,253 --> 00:32:12,131
The fuck? Is that Pat Parisi?

301
00:32:14,413 --> 00:32:16,483
Oh, shit!

302
00:32:20,853 --> 00:32:22,730
What should we do?

303
00:32:33,613 --> 00:32:34,932
He's drunk!

304
00:32:35,133 --> 00:32:38,443
- I told John, "Look... "
- Let's talk downstairs.

305
00:32:49,173 --> 00:32:51,368
Motherfucker.

306
00:32:52,893 --> 00:32:55,566
I don't understand this at all.

307
00:32:56,653 --> 00:32:59,292
Cocksucker.

308
00:33:15,453 --> 00:33:17,887
What's up, Ike?

309
00:33:18,773 --> 00:33:22,686
What happened at the Soprano house
was, the heater blew.

310
00:33:23,333 --> 00:33:26,564
Our unit saw Ruggerio
haul the old one out.

311
00:33:26,853 --> 00:33:30,482
- Ruggerio. A plumber?
- Why?

312
00:33:31,253 --> 00:33:34,609
My sister was friends
with Mrs. Ruggerio.

313
00:33:35,133 --> 00:33:38,887
Yeah, that's Mr. Ruggerio's
neighborhood.

314
00:33:39,253 --> 00:33:42,723
We have to get it in
before our warrant goes stale.

315
00:33:42,973 --> 00:33:47,683
Boy, we've had every one of Tony's
phones bugged for four years.

316
00:33:47,893 --> 00:33:52,967
- The guy says less than Harpo Marx.
- Next Tuesday the wire drop's a go.

317
00:33:57,573 --> 00:34:00,690
Der Bingle has left the building.

318
00:34:04,173 --> 00:34:05,970
They fucking made me.

319
00:34:06,573 --> 00:34:11,203
<i>- Wire drop is still a go.
- Confirming access to switching box.</i>

320
00:34:11,453 --> 00:34:13,284
I'm going in.

321
00:34:18,333 --> 00:34:21,882
Unit 2, Mrs. Bing in motion.

322
00:34:22,693 --> 00:34:26,402
<i>- Just the maid and it's yours, team.
- Copy that.</i>

323
00:34:28,373 --> 00:34:30,489
Siren wire is cut.

324
00:34:32,453 --> 00:34:35,604
The teacher knows nothing.

325
00:34:35,853 --> 00:34:40,529
Why do you quarrel with him always?
English is his first language...

326
00:34:40,773 --> 00:34:46,325
He waste our time with those
trick questions. "Stop. Men at work. "

327
00:34:46,573 --> 00:34:50,725
How do we know it doesn't mean,
"Stop all men who are working"?

328
00:34:50,973 --> 00:34:53,282
He shouldn't have taken a point.

329
00:34:53,533 --> 00:34:57,128
He thinks I'm a hack cabbie
from Pakistan.

330
00:34:57,373 --> 00:35:02,686
- Please, where are you going?
- I'm going back to work!

331
00:35:13,493 --> 00:35:15,324
- Excuse me?
- You scared me.

332
00:35:15,573 --> 00:35:19,282
Sorry. Is the West Essex
Language School around here?

333
00:35:19,533 --> 00:35:22,889
- There.
- Is it coed?

334
00:35:23,293 --> 00:35:26,524
- What?
- You wouldn't happen to be Polish?

335
00:35:27,133 --> 00:35:28,771
Yes.

336
00:35:29,333 --> 00:35:32,245
That's...
My grandmother is Polish.

337
00:35:42,133 --> 00:35:44,283
It's locked today.

338
00:35:48,693 --> 00:35:50,206
- Yes?
- My grandmother...

339
00:35:50,453 --> 00:35:53,923
Excuse me. How can I help you, sir?

340
00:35:54,173 --> 00:36:00,362
I was wondering if I could ask
you about the school. How is it?

341
00:36:00,573 --> 00:36:04,930
Sweet mother of Jesus!
Look at her today.

342
00:36:13,253 --> 00:36:15,005
Hi, Ade!

343
00:36:15,213 --> 00:36:17,488
Hi, guys. Be back in a second.

344
00:36:17,733 --> 00:36:21,282
Listen to this now. "Hi, Ade!"

345
00:36:22,213 --> 00:36:23,441
Hi!

346
00:36:24,373 --> 00:36:25,692
- Hi.
- Hey, you.

347
00:36:27,533 --> 00:36:30,331
- I love those.
- Yeah?

348
00:36:30,573 --> 00:36:32,211
Oh, my God.

349
00:36:32,453 --> 00:36:34,842
- Where'd you get them?
- Near my house.

350
00:36:47,133 --> 00:36:50,125
- This table's been moved.
- From the flood.

351
00:36:50,373 --> 00:36:53,888
It's not under the duct anymore.
Should we move it?

352
00:36:54,093 --> 00:36:59,486
- Two, three feet? Who's gonna notice?
- No, wait. Somebody might.

353
00:36:59,733 --> 00:37:05,285
But normal course of events, Tony
will assume Carmela moved it back.

354
00:37:05,493 --> 00:37:09,042
- If anybody even notices.
- Make an executive decision.

355
00:37:09,293 --> 00:37:13,172
- Grab an end.
- Easy.

356
00:37:13,373 --> 00:37:16,809
When she heard I was deferring,
she's like, "That's sketchy. "

357
00:37:17,053 --> 00:37:19,886
Are you serious?

358
00:37:20,133 --> 00:37:23,330
Eric Scatino hates Montclair.
He's doing acid.

359
00:37:23,573 --> 00:37:26,804
God, he was so straight-edge.
Hi, Caitlin.

360
00:37:27,373 --> 00:37:28,567
Hi.

361
00:37:28,773 --> 00:37:32,686
This is Hunter,
my friend I was telling you about.

362
00:37:38,773 --> 00:37:40,684
Wow.

363
00:37:41,453 --> 00:37:43,603
Do you like Citron Jell-O shots?

364
00:37:43,853 --> 00:37:46,925
- I haven't had any alcohol in a week.
- I know.

365
00:37:47,173 --> 00:37:53,169
I was gonna say we should go to
Panchito's, then I remembered. Bad idea.

366
00:37:54,213 --> 00:37:58,092
- I went to the health center.
- For that problem swallowing?

367
00:37:58,333 --> 00:38:00,642
They gave me BuSpar.

368
00:38:00,853 --> 00:38:03,606
That's for anxiety, right?

369
00:38:03,773 --> 00:38:05,604
I guess.

370
00:38:05,973 --> 00:38:08,885
There was this weight lifter
on the subway.

371
00:38:09,133 --> 00:38:15,083
He was eating chicken parts and
spitting bones back in the container.

372
00:38:15,733 --> 00:38:18,088
And the whole car reeked.

373
00:38:18,293 --> 00:38:23,128
This blind man sitting next to him,
you could tell he felt invaded.

374
00:38:23,373 --> 00:38:28,049
We all did.
Everybody just stared straight ahead.

375
00:38:28,853 --> 00:38:30,172
New York.

376
00:39:14,173 --> 00:39:15,811
Where is everybody?

377
00:39:20,693 --> 00:39:23,491
- What're you doing?
- Receipts from Sunday.

378
00:39:36,933 --> 00:39:39,401
- You got a problem?
- What, Ton?

379
00:39:39,733 --> 00:39:43,408
I said, "Do you got a problem?"

380
00:39:44,973 --> 00:39:50,286
- With what, Ton?
- I heard you got a problem being here.

381
00:39:50,733 --> 00:39:52,086
I like being here.

382
00:39:52,453 --> 00:39:54,728
- You're sure?
- Yeah.

383
00:39:55,093 --> 00:39:57,243
- You're sure?
- Yeah.

384
00:39:57,453 --> 00:40:00,684
Don't say you're sure
if you're not sure.

385
00:40:06,933 --> 00:40:12,690
You bought your daughter a nice house?
After you came over with us?

386
00:40:13,693 --> 00:40:17,322
- Yeah, that's nice.
- Wonderful thing.

387
00:40:22,293 --> 00:40:25,683
<i>And your brother, buon 'anima.</i>

388
00:40:26,693 --> 00:40:31,483
You've recovered from that shit?
You put your grief behind you?

389
00:40:38,693 --> 00:40:41,287
You put your grief behind you?

390
00:40:43,573 --> 00:40:45,882
Let me hear you say it.

391
00:40:49,453 --> 00:40:52,286
I put the grief behind me.

392
00:40:53,893 --> 00:40:56,885
I'm gonna go get a coffee and a bun.

393
00:41:02,293 --> 00:41:06,923
You got a younger son too?
You ought to bring him to the house.

394
00:41:07,173 --> 00:41:10,688
We can get something to eat,
they can go in the pool.

395
00:41:21,053 --> 00:41:26,081
We'll have to leave this junk on the
table. Don't know where to put it.

396
00:41:28,133 --> 00:41:29,725
Control, you hearing me?

397
00:41:29,973 --> 00:41:34,285
<i>- Loud and clear. Leave the factory.
- Roger that.</i>

398
00:41:39,133 --> 00:41:43,092
Wire's in, Bobby. I'm good to go.

399
00:41:44,173 --> 00:41:48,246
<i>- Control, we're in motion.
- Touchdown.</i>

400
00:41:48,453 --> 00:41:51,684
Dig, Soprano! Come on!
You wanna join the team?

401
00:41:51,933 --> 00:41:55,892
You think it's all for show
and not for go? Dig in.

402
00:41:56,093 --> 00:42:00,291
<i>You're out of there, George.
Unit 3, we're in.</i>

403
00:42:20,733 --> 00:42:24,089
<i>- So I got a job for you.
- Right.</i>

404
00:42:24,293 --> 00:42:27,603
<i>- Might get a little messy.
- I understand.</i>

405
00:42:27,853 --> 00:42:31,289
<i>- Wet work.
- All right.</i>

406
00:42:31,853 --> 00:42:37,086
<i>- I'll make it worth your while.
- I'm not worried.</i>

407
00:42:39,693 --> 00:42:43,288
<i>- Look over here.
- Minimization, 40 seconds.</i>

408
00:42:46,133 --> 00:42:52,049
- The old one flooded the whole place.
- I can smell the mildew, you know?

409
00:42:52,773 --> 00:42:56,482
You're an engineer.
I figured you could rig a system...

410
00:42:56,733 --> 00:43:00,282
...some PVC shit or something,
so if it happens again...

411
00:43:00,533 --> 00:43:04,208
...you get the overflow
and put it over to a sump pump.

412
00:43:04,453 --> 00:43:06,444
<i>Chip out the concrete.</i>

413
00:43:06,653 --> 00:43:09,167
- Four-0.
- They're not discussing OC.

414
00:43:14,573 --> 00:43:17,690
In two minutes
we're allowed to check back in.

415
00:43:22,173 --> 00:43:24,687
What do you think?

416
00:43:24,933 --> 00:43:26,810
Whatever.

417
00:43:27,013 --> 00:43:29,083
Well, how much?

418
00:43:29,653 --> 00:43:35,603
Time, materials...
I don't know how to concoct estimate.

419
00:43:35,813 --> 00:43:39,089
Well, fair enough.

420
00:43:39,333 --> 00:43:44,487
- Let me get measure. Get started.
- All right.

421
00:43:45,093 --> 00:43:48,085
- Hi, Stasiu.
- Hello.

422
00:43:50,653 --> 00:43:53,929
- You gonna use this?
- If you want it, take it.

423
00:43:54,173 --> 00:43:57,131
- No, you go ahead.
- Go ahead. I'll use the bike.

424
00:43:57,333 --> 00:44:00,325
I have to sort Meadow's laundry
anyway.

425
00:44:00,573 --> 00:44:03,645
Lilliana's making her a leg
of lamb to take.

426
00:44:03,853 --> 00:44:08,369
In Lodz, I had grant from the state
to do an autonomous research.

427
00:44:08,573 --> 00:44:11,610
Why don't you use it?
I'll take the bike.

428
00:44:11,813 --> 00:44:14,885
Jesus, already. No, you go ahead.

429
00:44:19,413 --> 00:44:23,691
Stas said he could smell
the mildew down here. Right, Stas?

430
00:44:25,373 --> 00:44:28,331
We've gotta let the place dry out.

431
00:44:37,093 --> 00:44:39,766
Got some girl
to take care of my mother.

432
00:44:39,973 --> 00:44:42,612
- Yeah, where'd you find her?
- Agency.

433
00:44:58,453 --> 00:45:00,887
<i>Good coffee this morning.</i>

434
00:45:01,773 --> 00:45:06,085
<i>Vienna Roast.
It's not as acidic as the Italian.</i>

435
00:45:06,733 --> 00:45:08,007
<i>Cleaned me out.</i>

436
00:45:08,253 --> 00:45:13,281
<i>What you need is more roughage
overall in your diet.</i>

437
00:45:14,213 --> 00:45:17,808
I've had something stuck
in my teeth for two days.

438
00:45:18,013 --> 00:45:20,891
You gotta use the other floss.

